From 70c003dc9c26fbf8cd5f5a67569bfd4390008559 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: riotashley81-jpg <riotashley81@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:06:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Frame interpolation: lock presents to the display's refresh
 grid

Presented on a host timer alone, the 60/s render-pass schedule beat against
a 120 Hz display: images stayed one or three refreshes instead of two, a
judder while the frame counter read 60. When the compositor reports its
vblank grid (Windows DWM) and the guest and output rates are within 2% of
whole refreshes, every deadline now sits half a refresh before a vblank,
re-snapped each interval so host-timer drift cannot walk it into the
boundary, and the swap waits for vblank. Off whole refreshes nothing changes.

Measured, Vagrant Story render passes at 60 on a 120 Hz panel, 2 x 3 runs:
images held two refreshes 39% -> 86%. PSX_INTERP_REFRESH_LOCK=0 turns it
off, 2 keeps vsync off. PSX_PRESENT_PACING=1 (TCP present_pacing) measures
refreshes per image and present lateness.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
